1
00:00:32,365 --> 00:00:39,372
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

2
00:00:58,391 --> 00:00:59,601
‎What are you doing here?

3
00:01:06,149 --> 00:01:07,025
‎Choi Jeong-yo.

4
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:12,030
‎Give me another chance.

5
00:01:15,366 --> 00:01:16,326
‎The performance…

6
00:01:18,119 --> 00:01:19,496
‎Let me do it.

7
00:01:24,417 --> 00:01:25,543
‎Don't be ridiculous.

8
00:01:29,088 --> 00:01:30,089
‎That piece.

9
00:01:31,299 --> 00:01:33,092
‎You wrote it out of pure hatred for me.

10
00:01:34,219 --> 00:01:35,178
‎Do you really think

11
00:01:35,845 --> 00:01:37,806
‎anyone else can actually play it right?

12
00:01:43,102 --> 00:01:44,354
‎Thanks, Jeong-yo.

13
00:01:45,563 --> 00:01:47,357
‎This experience made me realize my limits.

14
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:48,358
‎However,

15
00:01:49,025 --> 00:01:50,401
‎when it comes to ‎Nemesis‎,

16
00:01:51,861 --> 00:01:54,405
‎I know no one else
‎can do that piece justice.

17
00:01:55,698 --> 00:01:57,575
‎What's with this sudden ego?

18
00:01:59,536 --> 00:02:00,578
‎Listen.

19
00:02:01,746 --> 00:02:03,623
‎I‎ wrote ‎Nemesis‎.

20
00:02:04,791 --> 00:02:08,419
‎You and every other musician
‎are just tools.

21
00:02:10,171 --> 00:02:13,091
‎Choosing which tool to use
‎is entirely my right.

22
00:02:13,174 --> 00:02:14,050
‎You're wrong.

23
00:02:16,261 --> 00:02:19,139
‎You wrote ‎Nemesis‎ with me in mind
‎from the start.

24
00:02:20,223 --> 00:02:21,432
‎Once I get it right,

25
00:02:22,183 --> 00:02:24,102
‎the piece will finally be complete.

26
00:02:35,655 --> 00:02:37,157
‎Will you throw this chance away

27
00:02:37,782 --> 00:02:39,284
‎just for revenge?

28
00:02:41,244 --> 00:02:42,787
‎Cut the bullshit and get lost.

29
00:02:43,663 --> 00:02:45,915
‎You don't have the right
‎or the ability to play it.

30
00:03:21,409 --> 00:03:26,289
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

31
00:03:27,749 --> 00:03:29,083
‎EPISODE 11

32
00:03:29,167 --> 00:03:32,086
‎CERTIFICATE OF APPOINTMENT

33
00:03:38,343 --> 00:03:39,802
‎I'm here.

34
00:03:39,886 --> 00:03:41,179
‎Take as much time as you need.

35
00:03:50,355 --> 00:03:51,689
‎HAN HYUN-JEONG

36
00:03:54,943 --> 00:03:57,820
‎Ji-hye, how are you feeling?

37
00:03:58,446 --> 00:03:59,364
‎I'm fine.

38
00:04:00,323 --> 00:04:02,200
‎You had me so worried.

39
00:04:02,283 --> 00:04:04,077
‎No matter how much I called,
‎you wouldn't answer.

40
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:05,328
‎What is it?

41
00:04:05,995 --> 00:04:08,164
‎The thing is,

42
00:04:09,082 --> 00:04:10,708
‎it's about Pi-o's contract renewal.

43
00:04:10,792 --> 00:04:12,835
‎The company isn't doing well,

44
00:04:12,919 --> 00:04:15,171
‎so I think we'll need to reconsider it.

45
00:04:16,214 --> 00:04:17,507
‎I want an explanation.

46
00:04:19,092 --> 00:04:21,219
‎I'll just be honest then.

47
00:04:21,803 --> 00:04:25,640
‎We took a huge loss
‎because the album recording fell through.

48
00:04:25,723 --> 00:04:28,601
‎We let his slumps go unchecked until now,

49
00:04:28,685 --> 00:04:32,897
‎but when the album fell through,
‎people here have been talking a lot.

50
00:04:33,398 --> 00:04:36,276
‎So I don't think
‎we can renew his contract.

51
00:04:36,359 --> 00:04:39,404
‎I didn't want you
‎to hear this through Pi-o, so…

52
00:04:39,487 --> 00:04:40,571
‎Han Hyun-jeong.

53
00:04:41,823 --> 00:04:43,533
‎How could you do this to me?

54
00:04:44,117 --> 00:04:45,576
‎You saw it yourself.

55
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:48,788
‎You saw how Choi Jeong-yo
‎deliberately messed with Pi-o…

56
00:04:48,871 --> 00:04:51,874
‎Ji-hye, I don't know what to do either.

57
00:04:52,667 --> 00:04:55,378
‎There's no point in talking further

58
00:04:55,461 --> 00:04:57,005
‎because it'll upset us both.

59
00:04:58,506 --> 00:05:01,175
‎I don't feel good about
‎how things turned out.

60
00:05:01,259 --> 00:05:02,677
‎I just wanted to tell you

61
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:05,847
‎the staff will call Pi-o directly
‎with the details.

62
00:05:05,930 --> 00:05:07,223
‎I'll call you again later.

63
00:05:13,313 --> 00:05:14,814
‎What was that about?

64
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:18,860
‎You heard what I said. Why ask?

65
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:22,405
‎How could you even think about doing that?

66
00:05:23,573 --> 00:05:25,450
‎You know the state he's in right now,

67
00:05:25,533 --> 00:05:27,660
‎and you want us
‎to be the first to betray him?

68
00:05:28,578 --> 00:05:30,705
‎If we don't renew his contract over this,

69
00:05:30,788 --> 00:05:33,833
‎what artist would ever
‎feel safe signing with us?

70
00:05:33,916 --> 00:05:36,252
‎Isn't it our job as an agency
‎to trust the artist

71
00:05:36,336 --> 00:05:37,754
‎and help them through hard times?

72
00:05:38,338 --> 00:05:39,422
‎Just stay out of it.

73
00:05:40,423 --> 00:05:42,925
‎Something feels really off about them.

74
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:45,136
‎Don't you remember?

75
00:05:45,219 --> 00:05:46,512
‎After Jeong-yo had vanished,

76
00:05:46,596 --> 00:05:49,307
‎people whispered that Pi-o was behind it.

77
00:05:50,641 --> 00:05:51,851
‎You too, Mom?

78
00:05:52,894 --> 00:05:54,896
‎You can't accuse
‎an innocent person like that.

79
00:05:55,730 --> 00:05:57,732
‎And you can't presume to know him.

80
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:00,568
‎Don't you have any pride?

81
00:06:00,651 --> 00:06:03,905
‎You chased after him with a crush,
‎only for him to dump you.

82
00:06:03,988 --> 00:06:07,283
‎It's bad enough
‎that he dumped you like that!

83
00:06:07,366 --> 00:06:09,619
‎He has a murky past and no future.

84
00:06:09,702 --> 00:06:11,537
‎Why are you still siding with him?

85
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:17,126
‎I can't do this.

86
00:06:18,628 --> 00:06:19,462
‎I won't.

87
00:06:22,131 --> 00:06:24,175
‎I know what you're going to say.

88
00:06:24,258 --> 00:06:27,553
‎But if I turn myself in
‎while Pi-o is in that state,

89
00:06:27,637 --> 00:06:28,805
‎how will he…

90
00:06:29,889 --> 00:06:31,057
‎get back on his feet?

91
00:06:32,558 --> 00:06:34,769
‎Everyone's cutting ties with him as it is.

92
00:06:36,354 --> 00:06:38,106
‎If you don't renew Pi-o's contract,

93
00:06:38,815 --> 00:06:40,525
‎I'll quit the company.

94
00:06:40,608 --> 00:06:41,609
‎Got it?

95
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:47,532
‎Why are you always acting like a fool?

96
00:06:47,615 --> 00:06:48,574
‎Ji-hye.

97
00:06:50,034 --> 00:06:53,412
‎The longer you put this off,
‎the harder it'll be to come back.

98
00:06:54,622 --> 00:06:57,834
‎For everyone's sake, but especially yours,

99
00:06:58,751 --> 00:06:59,836
‎you need to be brave.

100
00:06:59,919 --> 00:07:02,255
‎I know that already.

101
00:07:03,714 --> 00:07:05,007
‎Give me some time.

102
00:07:07,343 --> 00:07:08,803
‎Just wait a little.

103
00:07:22,567 --> 00:07:24,819
‎Choi Jeong-yo, we need to talk.

104
00:07:25,486 --> 00:07:26,946
‎I'll come to your office.

105
00:07:32,618 --> 00:07:34,287
‎What brings you here?

106
00:07:34,954 --> 00:07:37,415
‎Choi Jeong-yo, tell me the truth.

107
00:07:38,749 --> 00:07:40,626
‎You're messing with Pi-o on purpose,
‎aren't you?

108
00:07:41,627 --> 00:07:42,795
‎"On purpose"?

109
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:45,923
‎Is it because of the rumor
‎that Pi-o was involved in your abduction?

110
00:07:46,841 --> 00:07:49,177
‎If so, then cut it out
‎because it's not true.

111
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:54,015
‎How can you be so sure?

112
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:55,558
‎So I was right.

113
00:07:56,767 --> 00:07:58,186
‎It was the rumor.

114
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:01,647
‎You know,

115
00:08:02,190 --> 00:08:05,109
‎I've watched both of you up close
‎longer than anyone.

116
00:08:06,486 --> 00:08:09,822
‎Pi-o was the only one who never gave up

117
00:08:09,906 --> 00:08:13,159
‎and searched everywhere in Europe for you.

118
00:08:13,659 --> 00:08:14,994
‎So how…

119
00:08:15,870 --> 00:08:19,457
‎How could you think the worst
‎of such a loyal friend over a rumor?

120
00:08:21,751 --> 00:08:23,336
‎Maybe he wasn't searching for me.

121
00:08:23,419 --> 00:08:26,589
‎It's possible he was checking
‎to see if I was dead.

122
00:08:27,173 --> 00:08:28,508
‎Wow, Choi Jeong-yo.

123
00:08:30,801 --> 00:08:32,345
‎I'm so disappointed in you.

124
00:08:32,845 --> 00:08:35,139
‎Pi-o couldn't get out of bed for days

125
00:08:35,223 --> 00:08:37,808
‎after hearing you were dead.

126
00:08:38,601 --> 00:08:40,728
‎I flew all the way to Moldova to get him.

127
00:08:41,312 --> 00:08:43,814
‎You'd been gone for ten years,
‎but when he heard you'd died,

128
00:08:43,898 --> 00:08:46,150
‎he couldn't even manage a sip of water.

129
00:08:47,235 --> 00:08:48,402
‎So how could you…

130
00:08:59,163 --> 00:08:59,997
‎Forget it.

131
00:09:00,623 --> 00:09:03,417
‎What more can I say to someone
‎who's using his amnesia as an excuse

132
00:09:04,001 --> 00:09:05,419
‎to blame an innocent person?

133
00:09:08,047 --> 00:09:09,006
‎In any case,

134
00:09:10,591 --> 00:09:12,301
‎if you keep going after Pi-o,

135
00:09:12,385 --> 00:09:15,513
‎I won't sit back and watch.

136
00:09:31,028 --> 00:09:32,363
‎HYUN-CHUL

137
00:09:32,446 --> 00:09:34,699
‎Why aren't you answering?
‎When do I release this?

138
00:09:38,452 --> 00:09:39,287
‎Just wait.

139
00:09:40,037 --> 00:09:41,163
‎Hold onto it for now.

140
00:10:00,558 --> 00:10:03,436
‎I've realized that music
‎that moves people's hearts

141
00:10:03,519 --> 00:10:05,396
‎is one that carries a lifetime within it.

142
00:10:09,191 --> 00:10:13,029
‎You said you wanted to play
‎even if you only had one day to live.

143
00:10:13,112 --> 00:10:16,115
‎Pour that resolve and your life
‎into your music.

144
00:10:30,212 --> 00:10:31,672
‎And here!

145
00:10:32,173 --> 00:10:35,843
‎This is written in marcato to convey
‎a sense of betrayal and vengeance.

146
00:10:35,926 --> 00:10:36,802
‎So…

147
00:10:37,887 --> 00:10:41,557
‎Do you really think
‎you're capturing any of these emotions?

148
00:10:41,641 --> 00:10:43,142
‎No, you're not!

149
00:10:49,398 --> 00:10:50,232
‎Mr. Kang.

150
00:10:53,027 --> 00:10:55,780
‎Don't forget we have to watch
‎the violinist videos at 3 p.m. today

151
00:10:55,863 --> 00:10:58,240
‎in the conference room
‎on the second floor.

152
00:10:59,075 --> 00:10:59,909
‎Right.

153
00:11:00,951 --> 00:11:04,330
‎Oh, and about my successor
‎for the artistic director role…

154
00:11:07,041 --> 00:11:08,501
‎Put that on hold for now.

155
00:11:10,586 --> 00:11:11,504
‎Really?

156
00:11:15,591 --> 00:11:16,801
‎May I ask why?

157
00:11:18,344 --> 00:11:20,721
‎Is something bothering you?

158
00:11:21,472 --> 00:11:23,516
‎I need to look into something.

159
00:11:24,809 --> 00:11:25,643
‎So just hold it off.

160
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:28,854
‎Okay.

161
00:11:56,465 --> 00:11:58,592
‎Are preparations for the premiere
‎coming together?

162
00:12:02,096 --> 00:12:03,222
‎Yes, well…

163
00:12:03,806 --> 00:12:05,724
‎I'm sure I don't have to tell you this,

164
00:12:06,934 --> 00:12:10,229
‎but a conductor must never
‎treat performers as mere tools.

165
00:12:11,439 --> 00:12:15,734
‎The stage belongs to the performers,
‎not the conductor.

166
00:12:16,652 --> 00:12:19,613
‎That's how you make
‎truly exceptional music.

167
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:25,286
‎I've been meaning to ask you something.

168
00:12:27,496 --> 00:12:28,789
‎Do you believe

169
00:12:29,748 --> 00:12:33,294
‎flawed artists don't deserve to make art?

170
00:12:33,377 --> 00:12:34,336
‎Or do you believe in

171
00:12:35,004 --> 00:12:38,716
‎separating the art from the artist?

172
00:12:39,633 --> 00:12:40,885
‎What do you mean?

173
00:12:40,968 --> 00:12:45,848
‎Art is supposed to be
‎a vessel for an artist's life.

174
00:12:47,308 --> 00:12:50,269
‎But if an artist commits
‎an unforgivable crime,

175
00:12:50,769 --> 00:12:54,023
‎is society obligated to accept their work?

176
00:12:54,857 --> 00:12:56,609
‎It's an age-old debate, isn't it?

177
00:12:57,318 --> 00:13:01,614
‎Are you trying to play judge,
‎or are you trying to be a musician?

178
00:13:06,327 --> 00:13:11,248
‎I don't think an artist's crime
‎taints their art.

179
00:13:12,708 --> 00:13:17,046
‎If anything, I believe
‎one must be flawed to make art.

180
00:13:18,005 --> 00:13:19,590
‎What we should be wary of

181
00:13:21,050 --> 00:13:24,762
‎is using art as an excuse
‎to commit evil deeds without remorse.

182
00:13:26,305 --> 00:13:29,558
‎Judging flawed artists
‎isn't our responsibility.

183
00:13:31,018 --> 00:13:34,313
‎An artist who commits
‎an unforgivable crime

184
00:13:34,396 --> 00:13:36,357
‎is going to be judged

185
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:38,609
‎for as long as their music lasts.

186
00:13:39,527 --> 00:13:41,737
‎Do you see that as a blessing

187
00:13:42,780 --> 00:13:44,532
‎or as a curse?

188
00:13:53,415 --> 00:13:56,168
‎I'm sorry. I had to take an urgent call.

189
00:13:56,252 --> 00:14:00,297
‎Shall we screen the applications
‎before watching the videos?

190
00:14:00,381 --> 00:14:01,674
‎Let's do that.

191
00:14:16,230 --> 00:14:19,024
‎Goodness, it's hard to find someone.

192
00:14:19,567 --> 00:14:21,860
‎They've all placed in major competitions,

193
00:14:21,944 --> 00:14:23,862
‎but none of them really…

194
00:15:09,116 --> 00:15:10,367
‎That tension you mentioned.

195
00:15:11,744 --> 00:15:12,870
‎Isn't this what you meant?

196
00:15:16,624 --> 00:15:18,250
‎What are you doing here?

197
00:15:19,335 --> 00:15:21,629
‎I'm sorry for letting myself in
‎while you were out.

198
00:15:21,712 --> 00:15:25,633
‎But unless you saw
‎the difference in me firsthand,

199
00:15:26,383 --> 00:15:28,052
‎I knew you wouldn't change your mind.

200
00:15:28,135 --> 00:15:30,137
‎You thought that would change my mind?

201
00:15:30,721 --> 00:15:31,555
‎So?

202
00:15:32,389 --> 00:15:33,849
‎Are you saying you didn't like it?

203
00:15:34,975 --> 00:15:36,435
‎Just admit it.

204
00:15:36,518 --> 00:15:38,854
‎The only person
‎who can do this piece justice

205
00:15:39,647 --> 00:15:40,773
‎is me.

206
00:16:37,579 --> 00:16:38,956
‎I've had a hunch for a while.

207
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:41,000
‎I take it

208
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:44,837
‎you have another pianist in mind
‎for this piece?

209
00:16:47,423 --> 00:16:48,465
‎What?

210
00:16:48,549 --> 00:16:50,175
‎Based on my years of experience,

211
00:16:51,135 --> 00:16:54,638
‎with premieres like this,
‎there's always someone it's meant for.

212
00:16:55,222 --> 00:16:58,183
‎But something tells me it's not me.

213
00:16:58,267 --> 00:16:59,935
‎If that's the case,

214
00:17:00,644 --> 00:17:03,439
‎you should go with that other person.

215
00:17:04,565 --> 00:17:05,482
‎That's not--

216
00:17:05,566 --> 00:17:06,483
‎It's understandable

217
00:17:07,109 --> 00:17:09,403
‎for a composer to go to any lengths
‎for their music.

218
00:17:24,585 --> 00:17:26,253
‎Based on my years of experience,

219
00:17:27,254 --> 00:17:30,841
‎with premieres like this,
‎there's always someone it's meant for.

220
00:17:35,387 --> 00:17:36,847
‎Just admit it.

221
00:17:38,057 --> 00:17:40,184
‎The only person
‎who can do this piece justice

222
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:42,603
‎is me.

223
00:17:43,729 --> 00:17:44,688
‎Mr. Choi.

224
00:17:53,489 --> 00:17:54,406
‎Who are you?

225
00:17:56,116 --> 00:17:58,035
‎Oh, I'm…

226
00:18:00,204 --> 00:18:01,830
‎It's me, you punk.

227
00:18:01,914 --> 00:18:03,290
‎You already know that.

228
00:18:09,463 --> 00:18:11,048
‎What is it you want to say?

229
00:18:11,131 --> 00:18:12,758
‎You can drop the act around me.

230
00:18:14,093 --> 00:18:16,637
‎I met Kang Pi-o's mom not long ago.

231
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:19,848
‎She seemed to be living well.

232
00:18:22,059 --> 00:18:24,728
‎You want to get revenge, don't you?

233
00:18:25,229 --> 00:18:26,522
‎But you know,

234
00:18:26,605 --> 00:18:29,358
‎you can't hold back
‎when it comes to revenge.

235
00:18:30,526 --> 00:18:32,444
‎When you take someone down,

236
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:35,864
‎you swoop in and crush them completely
‎so they can't retaliate.

237
00:18:35,948 --> 00:18:37,282
‎You've got to make it public too.

238
00:18:38,617 --> 00:18:39,618
‎Want some help?

239
00:18:47,584 --> 00:18:49,628
‎Are you still up to the same shit?

240
00:18:51,463 --> 00:18:53,215
‎Who said you could mess with him?

241
00:18:54,258 --> 00:18:56,218
‎Only I get to do that.

242
00:18:57,136 --> 00:18:59,221
‎If you lay a finger on Kang Pi-o,

243
00:18:59,888 --> 00:19:01,723
‎I'll kill you first.

244
00:19:02,516 --> 00:19:03,559
‎Understand?

245
00:19:08,981 --> 00:19:11,483
‎Man, you almost broke my wrist.

246
00:19:12,651 --> 00:19:13,610
‎Damages, please.

247
00:19:18,532 --> 00:19:19,491
‎Damn.

248
00:19:21,118 --> 00:19:22,703
‎I bring up Kang Pi-o, and you lose it.

249
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:25,247
‎You've gotten pretty ruthless, Jeong-yo.

250
00:19:25,914 --> 00:19:26,874
‎Good for you.

251
00:19:29,084 --> 00:19:30,210
‎Good luck, you punk.

252
00:19:59,072 --> 00:19:59,990
‎Come outside.

253
00:20:00,657 --> 00:20:01,658
‎I'm at your house.

254
00:20:09,666 --> 00:20:11,210
‎Do the performance.

255
00:20:12,294 --> 00:20:14,630
‎But this doesn't mean
‎I forgive you completely.

256
00:20:15,422 --> 00:20:16,381
‎I'm only doing this

257
00:20:17,174 --> 00:20:19,468
‎because I want ‎Nemesis‎ to be perfect.

258
00:20:31,021 --> 00:20:35,067
‎NEMESIS
‎A MESSAGE FROM THE FUTURE

259
00:20:40,113 --> 00:20:42,658
‎HANKOOK SYMPHONY 80TH ANNIVERSARY CONCERT
‎A MESSAGE FROM THE FUTURE: NEMESIS

260
00:22:09,745 --> 00:22:11,663
‎Greetings, everyone.

261
00:22:12,164 --> 00:22:14,750
‎I'm Yoon Seon-ju,
‎the head of the Hankook Symphony.

262
00:22:14,833 --> 00:22:19,921
‎Thank you for attending
‎our symphony's 80th anniversary festival…

263
00:22:37,272 --> 00:22:39,941
‎I hope this stays with everyone
‎for years to come.

264
00:22:40,025 --> 00:22:42,110
‎Let the performance begin.

265
00:25:20,310 --> 00:25:22,020
‎You think your opinion matters right now?

266
00:25:22,103 --> 00:25:24,314
‎Hey. You'll never beat me.

267
00:25:29,110 --> 00:25:31,613
‎You chase it down,
‎only for it to move farther away.

268
00:25:32,197 --> 00:25:33,907
‎When you pursue it again,

269
00:25:33,990 --> 00:25:35,116
‎it moves even farther.

270
00:25:35,784 --> 00:25:38,870
‎Do you still want to
‎go down this thorny road?

271
00:25:40,997 --> 00:25:44,042
‎If you had less than a month to live,

272
00:25:44,125 --> 00:25:46,294
‎would you still want to play the piano?

273
00:25:49,256 --> 00:25:51,341
‎I'm only happy when I play the piano.

274
00:25:52,467 --> 00:25:54,344
‎Even if I only had one day left to live,

275
00:25:54,427 --> 00:25:56,221
‎I'd still want to play the piano.

276
00:26:31,298 --> 00:26:33,925
‎Command the stage with your energy.

277
00:26:34,759 --> 00:26:36,386
‎If your energy is strong enough,

278
00:26:36,469 --> 00:26:41,057
‎you can pull the conductor
‎and the orchestra into your orbit.

279
00:28:16,861 --> 00:28:17,946
‎You were right.

280
00:28:19,614 --> 00:28:21,950
‎This piece was meant entirely for you.

281
00:29:56,711 --> 00:29:59,297
‎I'm truly grateful
‎to everyone in the audience

282
00:29:59,380 --> 00:30:01,174
‎for joining us at today's concert.

283
00:30:01,674 --> 00:30:05,887
‎It was an absolute honor for me
‎to perform ‎Nemesis‎,

284
00:30:06,429 --> 00:30:09,182
‎Conductor Choi Jeong-yo's masterpiece.

285
00:30:11,559 --> 00:30:12,477
‎However,

286
00:30:14,354 --> 00:30:15,647
‎I want to take this moment…

287
00:30:17,482 --> 00:30:19,108
‎to make a confession.

288
00:30:24,948 --> 00:30:26,074
‎The truth is…

289
00:30:28,701 --> 00:30:31,120
‎I have no right to be standing here.

290
00:30:33,414 --> 00:30:34,249
‎Nine years ago,

291
00:30:35,625 --> 00:30:38,545
‎an abduction occurred
‎during the Prague Harmonie Competition.

292
00:30:41,047 --> 00:30:43,842
‎The one who ordered
‎Conductor Choi Jeong-yo's abduction was…

293
00:30:48,012 --> 00:30:50,974
‎was me.

294
00:30:58,231 --> 00:30:59,440
‎As a result,

295
00:30:59,941 --> 00:31:02,068
‎I've held an honor that was never mine

296
00:31:03,111 --> 00:31:04,904
‎for nearly ten years.

297
00:31:07,866 --> 00:31:11,160
‎I offer my sincere apologies
‎to Conductor Choi Jeong-yo,

298
00:31:12,370 --> 00:31:14,539
‎who suffered because of me.

299
00:31:15,582 --> 00:31:17,000
‎Therefore, as of today,

300
00:31:18,084 --> 00:31:20,545
‎I'm walking away
‎from everything I've been given

301
00:31:20,628 --> 00:31:23,089
‎and accepting the punishment I deserve.

302
00:31:23,172 --> 00:31:26,050
‎To everyone in the audience
‎who has supported me,

303
00:31:27,510 --> 00:31:28,803
‎I am deeply sorry…

304
00:31:32,432 --> 00:31:34,225
‎for disappointing you.

305
00:31:42,483 --> 00:31:44,819
‎-What on earth?
‎-He's finished for good.

306
00:32:09,260 --> 00:32:11,304
‎-Why perform at all?
‎-Is he serious?

307
00:32:16,184 --> 00:32:17,101
‎You bastard.

308
00:32:18,519 --> 00:32:20,063
‎What do you think you're doing?

309
00:32:20,939 --> 00:32:22,065
‎I'm sorry.

310
00:32:23,107 --> 00:32:24,192
‎And thank you.

311
00:32:25,109 --> 00:32:26,402
‎It took me until today…

312
00:32:28,404 --> 00:32:30,073
‎to finally understand you.

313
00:32:30,657 --> 00:32:32,158
‎What the hell are you saying?

314
00:32:32,742 --> 00:32:33,785
‎Mr. Kang?

315
00:32:35,203 --> 00:32:38,915
‎I'm Inspector Han from Major Crimes.
‎I'm with Seoul Central Police.

316
00:32:39,832 --> 00:32:42,460
‎Please come down to the station with us.

317
00:32:48,716 --> 00:32:51,844
‎Wait, I think there's been
‎a misunderstanding.

318
00:32:51,928 --> 00:32:54,347
‎Hold on. Pi-o, you need to explain this.

319
00:32:54,430 --> 00:32:55,682
‎Was that all true?

320
00:32:55,765 --> 00:32:57,517
‎Pi-o!

321
00:32:57,600 --> 00:32:59,602
‎Wait, please!

322
00:32:59,686 --> 00:33:00,645
‎Please!

323
00:33:00,728 --> 00:33:03,648
‎-Who knew Kang Pi-o had done that?
‎-But he actually got arrested.

324
00:33:03,731 --> 00:33:06,150
‎-I know. Something definitely happened.
‎-I guess so.

325
00:33:20,456 --> 00:33:22,583
‎KANG PI-O MAKES SHOCKING CONFESSION
‎REGARDING 9-YEAR-OLD COLD CASE

326
00:33:22,667 --> 00:33:24,627
‎What's going on? Is that true?

327
00:33:24,711 --> 00:33:26,838
‎KANG PI-O CONFESSES TO INVOLVEMENT
‎IN CHOI JEONG-YO'S ABDUCTION

328
00:33:26,921 --> 00:33:28,965
‎THE TRUTH BEHIND THE SUCCESS:
‎KANG PI-O CONTROVERSY ESCALATES

329
00:33:29,048 --> 00:33:31,968
‎-So he really was behind it?
‎-What on earth?

330
00:33:32,635 --> 00:33:34,929
‎CALLING KANG JI-HYE

331
00:33:42,520 --> 00:33:44,480
‎Why isn't she answering?

332
00:33:49,736 --> 00:33:50,987
‎Excuse me.

333
00:33:51,070 --> 00:33:53,531
‎Can you tell me where Kang Pi-o
‎is being questioned?

334
00:33:53,614 --> 00:33:56,117
‎No visits are allowed during questioning.

335
00:34:00,705 --> 00:34:02,957
‎I need to see the detective in charge.

336
00:34:03,041 --> 00:34:04,292
‎I'll tell them everything.

337
00:34:04,375 --> 00:34:05,376
‎I did it.

338
00:34:06,127 --> 00:34:07,253
‎It was all me.

339
00:34:07,336 --> 00:34:09,047
‎My son is innocent.

340
00:34:09,630 --> 00:34:11,174
‎I get what you're saying,

341
00:34:11,257 --> 00:34:14,218
‎but no visits are allowed
‎during questioning.

342
00:34:14,802 --> 00:34:15,928
‎Go home for now,

343
00:34:16,888 --> 00:34:19,182
‎and request a visit
‎once the questioning is over.

344
00:34:19,265 --> 00:34:20,600
‎But I did it.

345
00:34:20,683 --> 00:34:22,602
‎Arrest me instead, detective.

346
00:34:23,102 --> 00:34:24,520
‎-Ms. Kang.
‎-Jae-in.

347
00:34:26,230 --> 00:34:27,482
‎What should I do?

348
00:34:28,066 --> 00:34:29,400
‎You know, don't you?

349
00:34:29,484 --> 00:34:30,818
‎I know you do.

350
00:34:31,694 --> 00:34:33,404
‎You know Pi-o didn't do it.

351
00:34:34,280 --> 00:34:35,281
‎It was all me.

352
00:34:37,408 --> 00:34:38,785
‎-It was…
‎-Ms. Kang.

353
00:34:57,678 --> 00:34:58,971
‎Let me see him.

354
00:34:59,639 --> 00:35:01,057
‎I'm sorry,

355
00:35:01,140 --> 00:35:03,851
‎but you can't have a one-on-one
‎with the suspect.

356
00:35:03,935 --> 00:35:04,769
‎No.

357
00:35:07,605 --> 00:35:08,856
‎Let me see him.

358
00:35:12,735 --> 00:35:14,862
‎Give me a minute then.

359
00:35:27,834 --> 00:35:28,876
‎What are you doing?

360
00:35:31,712 --> 00:35:32,839
‎You…

361
00:35:36,092 --> 00:35:37,802
‎You ruined everything. Do you get that?

362
00:35:39,762 --> 00:35:42,932
‎Do you have any idea
‎how hard I've fought to keep going?

363
00:35:45,143 --> 00:35:45,977
‎Do you…

364
00:35:48,813 --> 00:35:51,149
‎Do you really think
‎this is how I wanted it to end?

365
00:35:52,775 --> 00:35:56,154
‎I said I'm the only one
‎who gets to judge you or kill you.

366
00:35:56,237 --> 00:35:57,864
‎-So why the hell--
‎-I'm sorry.

367
00:35:59,365 --> 00:36:01,659
‎This was the best I could do for you.

368
00:36:03,327 --> 00:36:06,330
‎You're far too gifted to waste your time

369
00:36:07,290 --> 00:36:09,458
‎on this futile revenge.

370
00:36:11,377 --> 00:36:13,171
‎So let go of your hate…

371
00:36:15,798 --> 00:36:16,799
‎and focus on your music.

372
00:36:19,177 --> 00:36:20,928
‎-Hey.
‎-Mr. Choi.

373
00:36:21,012 --> 00:36:23,097
‎-Who do you think you are?
‎-That's enough.

374
00:36:23,181 --> 00:36:25,433
‎Who the hell are you to lecture me?

375
00:36:25,516 --> 00:36:27,852
‎-Step outside, now.
‎-What gives you the right?

376
00:36:42,450 --> 00:36:44,577
‎HYUN-CHUL

377
00:36:45,620 --> 00:36:46,579
‎Damn it.

378
00:36:47,413 --> 00:36:50,124
‎Where are you? Why aren't you answering?

379
00:37:12,521 --> 00:37:14,565
‎What did the police say?

380
00:37:16,192 --> 00:37:17,360
‎It can't be true.

381
00:37:19,362 --> 00:37:20,821
‎They made a mistake, right?

382
00:37:22,281 --> 00:37:23,199
‎It's not true.

383
00:37:24,992 --> 00:37:26,285
‎Pi-o didn't do it.

384
00:37:27,161 --> 00:37:29,622
‎Then why did Pi-o say that?

385
00:37:30,539 --> 00:37:32,166
‎Because I did it.

386
00:37:36,504 --> 00:37:37,797
‎What do you mean?

387
00:37:39,340 --> 00:37:40,383
‎It wasn't Pi-o.

388
00:37:41,550 --> 00:37:43,261
‎I ordered the abduction.

389
00:37:49,976 --> 00:37:51,227
‎You were behind it?

390
00:37:52,395 --> 00:37:53,479
‎That's right.

391
00:37:53,562 --> 00:37:54,397
‎It was me.

392
00:37:55,356 --> 00:37:56,983
‎I ordered the abduction

393
00:37:57,984 --> 00:37:59,360
‎so Pi-o could win first place!

394
00:38:00,945 --> 00:38:01,821
‎You…

395
00:38:04,240 --> 00:38:05,324
‎You're not even human.

396
00:38:06,117 --> 00:38:09,203
‎How could you do something so vile?

397
00:38:10,830 --> 00:38:12,623
‎This is all your fault, Father.

398
00:38:14,000 --> 00:38:17,795
‎If you had been kind to Pi-o,
‎I wouldn't have done it.

399
00:38:18,504 --> 00:38:21,048
‎If only you had acknowledged him,

400
00:38:21,132 --> 00:38:23,342
‎I wouldn't have done something this crazy!

401
00:38:23,426 --> 00:38:24,802
‎How could you do that?

402
00:38:24,885 --> 00:38:26,304
‎How could you do that to me?

403
00:38:26,387 --> 00:38:27,596
‎How could you do that to Pi-o?

404
00:38:27,680 --> 00:38:29,181
‎Explain yourself!

405
00:38:29,265 --> 00:38:32,518
‎How could you do that?

406
00:38:36,314 --> 00:38:38,065
‎How could you?

407
00:38:38,149 --> 00:38:41,694
‎How could you do that, Father?

408
00:39:03,674 --> 00:39:04,508
‎I'm here…

409
00:39:05,926 --> 00:39:07,636
‎to turn myself in.

410
00:39:08,512 --> 00:39:10,139
‎I did it.

411
00:39:10,222 --> 00:39:12,016
‎My son didn't know anything.

412
00:39:13,893 --> 00:39:15,561
‎He found out the truth only recently,

413
00:39:16,354 --> 00:39:18,064
‎and he took the fall for me…

414
00:39:19,982 --> 00:39:21,609
‎to protect me.

415
00:39:24,653 --> 00:39:26,238
‎If you check his phone…

416
00:39:27,990 --> 00:39:31,577
‎you'll find a photo of me
‎meeting with the abductor.

417
00:39:31,660 --> 00:39:32,620
‎Look for it.

418
00:39:32,703 --> 00:39:33,954
‎I'm sorry,

419
00:39:34,663 --> 00:39:38,084
‎but there was no such photo on his phone.

420
00:39:39,919 --> 00:39:41,504
‎-That can't be.
‎-Ma'am.

421
00:39:41,587 --> 00:39:42,963
‎Your son

422
00:39:43,964 --> 00:39:47,218
‎has handed over conclusive evidence

423
00:39:47,301 --> 00:39:49,387
‎proving his ongoing contact
‎with the abductors.

424
00:39:49,970 --> 00:39:50,930
‎We also have proof

425
00:39:51,806 --> 00:39:54,642
‎that he took out a large sum in Moldova

426
00:39:55,476 --> 00:39:57,061
‎to give to the abductors.

427
00:39:59,897 --> 00:40:00,856
‎Ma'am.

428
00:40:01,774 --> 00:40:03,401
‎No matter what you do,

429
00:40:03,484 --> 00:40:06,445
‎you can't take the blame
‎for your son's crime.

430
00:40:06,529 --> 00:40:08,781
‎Please stop interfering
‎with the investigation

431
00:40:09,532 --> 00:40:10,658
‎and go home.

432
00:40:11,242 --> 00:40:13,411
‎But I really did it.

433
00:40:14,578 --> 00:40:16,956
‎Please believe me.

434
00:40:17,957 --> 00:40:19,291
‎It was me.

435
00:40:42,940 --> 00:40:44,024
‎Jeong-yo.

436
00:40:45,234 --> 00:40:46,360
‎Forgive me.

437
00:40:48,529 --> 00:40:50,573
‎It wasn't Pi-o who ordered your abduction.

438
00:40:51,907 --> 00:40:52,992
‎It was me.

439
00:40:54,034 --> 00:40:56,120
‎I lost my mind for a moment

440
00:40:57,121 --> 00:40:58,998
‎and did something horrible to you.

441
00:41:01,876 --> 00:41:05,212
‎Pi-o had no idea
‎until he found out recently.

442
00:41:06,964 --> 00:41:09,258
‎He wanted me to ask for your forgiveness,

443
00:41:10,176 --> 00:41:12,553
‎but I refused
‎and threatened to kill myself.

444
00:41:14,680 --> 00:41:16,223
‎That's how I kept him from coming.

445
00:41:18,476 --> 00:41:20,603
‎Yet Pi-o still sees me as his mother,

446
00:41:22,229 --> 00:41:25,357
‎and he's trying to take the fall for me.

447
00:41:25,441 --> 00:41:26,442
‎Jeong-yo.

448
00:41:27,276 --> 00:41:29,195
‎Can you tell them your memory is back?

449
00:41:30,529 --> 00:41:34,742
‎Can you give a statement
‎saying I'm the one who did it, not Pi-o?

450
00:41:36,577 --> 00:41:37,828
‎Of course,

451
00:41:38,662 --> 00:41:41,081
‎I know how much you must resent me.

452
00:41:41,916 --> 00:41:45,544
‎But you're the only person
‎I could turn to for help.

453
00:41:47,671 --> 00:41:49,006
‎I'll face the punishment.

454
00:41:49,632 --> 00:41:51,258
‎Just save my son.

455
00:41:54,220 --> 00:41:56,180
‎You expect me to believe that?

456
00:42:00,226 --> 00:42:02,561
‎I understand your urge
‎to protect your son.

457
00:42:04,688 --> 00:42:06,899
‎But must you go this far?

458
00:42:08,108 --> 00:42:10,736
‎And to someone
‎whose life he ruined, no less.

459
00:42:15,324 --> 00:42:17,368
‎Please go home, or I'll call the police.

460
00:42:17,451 --> 00:42:18,869
‎No!

461
00:42:19,453 --> 00:42:20,371
‎Please believe me.

462
00:42:20,454 --> 00:42:22,373
‎You must believe me, Jeong-yo.

463
00:42:22,456 --> 00:42:25,251
‎I did it. It was all me.

464
00:42:25,334 --> 00:42:28,170
‎Pi-o didn't know anything!

465
00:42:28,254 --> 00:42:30,297
‎Jeong-yo!

466
00:42:30,381 --> 00:42:32,049
‎Jeong-yo!

467
00:42:32,800 --> 00:42:34,677
‎Jeong-yo, please listen to me.

468
00:42:36,428 --> 00:42:37,346
‎I'm sorry.

469
00:42:38,806 --> 00:42:39,890
‎I'm so sorry.

470
00:42:41,725 --> 00:42:43,477
‎It's all my fault.

471
00:42:45,020 --> 00:42:46,772
‎Pi-o was your friend.

472
00:42:47,439 --> 00:42:50,859
‎Hate me all you want,
‎but please don't hate Pi-o.

473
00:42:52,528 --> 00:42:55,072
‎Please, Jeong-yo…

474
00:42:57,825 --> 00:42:59,660
‎During the one-on-one,

475
00:43:00,494 --> 00:43:01,662
‎it sounded like

476
00:43:02,454 --> 00:43:06,917
‎you were telling the suspect
‎that you already knew he was guilty.

477
00:43:07,001 --> 00:43:08,168
‎Is it true?

478
00:43:09,253 --> 00:43:10,379
‎I'm sorry.

479
00:43:11,380 --> 00:43:12,506
‎And thank you.

480
00:43:13,424 --> 00:43:14,717
‎It took me until today…

481
00:43:16,677 --> 00:43:18,387
‎to finally understand you.

482
00:43:19,013 --> 00:43:20,931
‎This was the best I could do for you.

483
00:43:23,017 --> 00:43:26,145
‎You're far too gifted to waste your time

484
00:43:26,729 --> 00:43:28,397
‎on this futile revenge.

485
00:43:30,316 --> 00:43:32,151
‎So let go of your hate…

486
00:43:34,778 --> 00:43:35,738
‎and focus on your music.

487
00:43:45,289 --> 00:43:46,123
‎No.

488
00:43:46,957 --> 00:43:47,791
‎No, it's not.

489
00:43:49,835 --> 00:43:51,295
‎I have no memory of it.

490
00:43:53,172 --> 00:43:54,340
‎Right.

491
00:43:54,423 --> 00:43:57,176
‎Then what were you talking about?

492
00:43:57,843 --> 00:43:59,970
‎The part about how Kang Pi-o
‎ordered your abduction.

493
00:44:00,679 --> 00:44:01,555
‎I just…

494
00:44:07,269 --> 00:44:09,104
‎I just heard a rumor about it.

495
00:44:41,679 --> 00:44:42,554
‎Mr. Choi?

496
00:44:45,099 --> 00:44:46,100
‎Choi Jeong-yo, right?

497
00:44:54,608 --> 00:44:55,651
‎Hello, Mr. Choi.

498
00:44:57,111 --> 00:44:59,613
‎I have something to tell you
‎about Kang Pi-o.

499
00:45:00,322 --> 00:45:01,407
‎Can we talk?

500
00:45:02,574 --> 00:45:04,493
‎Right, you don't know who I am.

501
00:45:04,576 --> 00:45:06,036
‎But I'm very familiar with you.

502
00:45:07,162 --> 00:45:09,623
‎I'm so glad we finally got to meet.

503
00:45:10,207 --> 00:45:11,750
‎What do you want to tell me?

504
00:45:12,251 --> 00:45:13,210
‎The thing is,

505
00:45:14,753 --> 00:45:15,754
‎Mr. Kang

506
00:45:17,005 --> 00:45:19,299
‎was never the one
‎who ordered your abduction.

507
00:45:19,925 --> 00:45:22,511
‎If anything, he prayed day and night
‎that you were still alive.

508
00:45:24,304 --> 00:45:26,473
‎What are you saying?

509
00:45:26,557 --> 00:45:30,060
‎Did you know Mr. Kang
‎spent five long years searching for you?

510
00:45:31,145 --> 00:45:32,729
‎I'm the one who looked into your case.

511
00:45:34,398 --> 00:45:35,399
‎So?

512
00:45:36,692 --> 00:45:40,737
‎How do you know if he was checking
‎whether I was dead or still alive?

513
00:45:41,321 --> 00:45:44,283
‎Because I saw how he reacted
‎when he heard you were dead.

514
00:45:45,659 --> 00:45:47,661
‎Mr. Kang was distraught.

515
00:45:49,371 --> 00:45:51,081
‎Did his mother tell you to come here?

516
00:45:52,124 --> 00:45:54,668
‎Why on earth are you telling such a lie?

517
00:45:55,878 --> 00:45:59,173
‎Do I look stupid enough
‎to fall for these games?

518
00:46:03,260 --> 00:46:04,678
‎When we met with the abductor,

519
00:46:05,888 --> 00:46:07,639
‎I had my recorder on.

520
00:46:14,104 --> 00:46:16,273
‎You'll hear Mr. Kang's true feelings here.

521
00:46:29,495 --> 00:46:32,706
‎Why did you kill him?

522
00:46:33,665 --> 00:46:34,917
‎Was it for money?

523
00:46:35,000 --> 00:46:37,002
‎Did you abduct him for that reason
‎or did someone--

524
00:46:37,085 --> 00:46:38,045
‎Enough.

525
00:46:38,128 --> 00:46:39,296
‎You want to know?

526
00:46:40,297 --> 00:46:41,673
‎Three million lei.

527
00:46:41,757 --> 00:46:42,841
‎Then I'll tell you.

528
00:46:45,302 --> 00:46:46,178
‎Tell me now!

529
00:46:46,261 --> 00:46:47,846
‎Mr. Kang, no!

530
00:46:47,930 --> 00:46:49,515
‎You killed someone over money?

531
00:46:49,598 --> 00:46:50,891
‎Do you even know how special he was?

532
00:46:50,974 --> 00:46:52,643
‎Do you have any idea?

533
00:46:52,726 --> 00:46:53,810
‎Stop!

534
00:46:59,274 --> 00:47:01,068
‎Do you know who we are?

535
00:47:01,944 --> 00:47:02,861
‎You little…

536
00:47:03,362 --> 00:47:04,488
‎You know what?

537
00:47:05,280 --> 00:47:08,158
‎Now, six million.

538
00:47:08,242 --> 00:47:09,076
‎Then I'll tell you.

539
00:47:09,159 --> 00:47:12,287
‎Then I saw you hand over money
‎to another one.

540
00:47:12,371 --> 00:47:14,915
‎Where's the nearest international bank?

541
00:47:36,228 --> 00:47:38,021
‎MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE

542
00:48:25,027 --> 00:48:27,946
‎CHOI JEONG-YO

543
00:48:32,743 --> 00:48:36,955
‎I'VE MEMORIZED EVERYTHING.
‎TAKE IT IF YOU NEED IT!

544
00:48:37,039 --> 00:48:39,750
‎Come back, Jeong-yo.

545
00:49:26,254 --> 00:49:27,798
‎Come on out, Mr. Kang.

546
00:49:29,299 --> 00:49:30,550
‎You're free to go.

547
00:49:32,177 --> 00:49:33,887
‎Why are you letting me go?

548
00:49:34,388 --> 00:49:37,391
‎Did my mother say she did it
‎and turn herself in?

549
00:49:39,309 --> 00:49:40,852
‎Let me explain.

550
00:49:40,936 --> 00:49:44,314
‎It seems she fabricated evidence
‎to take the fall for me,

551
00:49:44,398 --> 00:49:45,607
‎but she's innocent.

552
00:49:45,691 --> 00:49:47,859
‎Don't believe her. I did it, so--

553
00:49:47,943 --> 00:49:48,819
‎Look.

554
00:49:50,487 --> 00:49:52,823
‎That's enough, Mr. Kang.

555
00:49:52,906 --> 00:49:57,369
‎We've got all the evidence
‎proving you didn't do it.

556
00:49:58,995 --> 00:50:00,038
‎And the victim

557
00:50:01,123 --> 00:50:03,458
‎gave a statement saying you didn't do it.

558
00:50:08,463 --> 00:50:11,383
‎Do you admit to ordering
‎Choi Jeong-yo's abduction?

559
00:50:12,759 --> 00:50:13,593
‎Yes.

560
00:50:14,428 --> 00:50:15,470
‎I admit it.

561
00:50:16,513 --> 00:50:18,515
‎When did you meet the abductors?

562
00:50:19,224 --> 00:50:22,144
‎On March 18th, 2017.

563
00:50:22,769 --> 00:50:26,022
‎I believe it was near
‎Wenceslas Square in Prague.

564
00:50:30,152 --> 00:50:32,487
‎SEOUL CENTRAL POLICE STATION

565
00:51:33,715 --> 00:51:34,549
‎Are you okay?

566
00:51:38,053 --> 00:51:39,554
‎I'm sorry, Pi-o.

567
00:51:40,597 --> 00:51:42,516
‎I had no idea what you were dealing with

568
00:51:43,892 --> 00:51:46,853
‎and spent all this time
‎resenting and hating you.

569
00:51:47,771 --> 00:51:50,941
‎Still, I wish you would've told me.

570
00:51:51,900 --> 00:51:53,735
‎You didn't have to go through it alone.

571
00:51:54,319 --> 00:51:55,403
‎You should've told me.

572
00:51:56,613 --> 00:51:58,323
‎I'm sorry, Jae-in…

573
00:52:00,742 --> 00:52:02,202
‎for being so pathetic.

574
00:52:13,630 --> 00:52:14,548
‎Kang Pi-o.

575
00:52:24,641 --> 00:52:25,851
‎Why did you do it?

576
00:52:28,270 --> 00:52:29,354
‎I heard everything.

577
00:52:31,815 --> 00:52:33,567
‎You should've told me from the start.

578
00:52:36,862 --> 00:52:38,154
‎You should've been honest…

579
00:52:40,448 --> 00:52:42,701
‎and said you didn't do it.

580
00:52:43,952 --> 00:52:45,245
‎I'm sorry.

581
00:52:45,829 --> 00:52:46,663
‎But…

582
00:52:49,332 --> 00:52:50,792
‎even if I didn't do it,

583
00:52:52,085 --> 00:52:54,087
‎I can't say I hadn't thought about it.

584
00:52:56,089 --> 00:52:57,507
‎Even if my mom hadn't tried it…

585
00:52:59,759 --> 00:53:02,345
‎I would've wanted to
‎get rid of you at some point.

586
00:53:04,723 --> 00:53:06,641
‎That's how a lifetime runner-up thinks.

587
00:53:42,802 --> 00:53:43,887
‎Why did you do it?

588
00:53:44,429 --> 00:53:45,472
‎What about you?

589
00:53:46,598 --> 00:53:47,807
‎You made a fool out of me.

590
00:53:48,808 --> 00:53:50,310
‎Because it was all my fault.

591
00:53:51,770 --> 00:53:52,771
‎You know…

592
00:53:55,023 --> 00:53:57,901
‎I've always liked seeing you smile
‎since I was a kid.

593
00:53:58,401 --> 00:54:01,988
‎So I wanted to do everything I could
‎to make you smile.

594
00:54:03,490 --> 00:54:05,075
‎When I won my first competition

595
00:54:06,534 --> 00:54:09,454
‎and saw you smile so brightly,

596
00:54:10,455 --> 00:54:11,456
‎I thought,

597
00:54:13,083 --> 00:54:14,376
‎"This is it."

598
00:54:16,670 --> 00:54:18,755
‎"My mom is proud of me."

599
00:54:19,673 --> 00:54:21,174
‎"She isn't ashamed…

600
00:54:23,134 --> 00:54:24,594
‎but proud of me."

601
00:54:26,179 --> 00:54:27,222
‎In the end,

602
00:54:28,640 --> 00:54:30,767
‎I think I made you this way.

603
00:54:31,893 --> 00:54:32,769
‎Kang Pi-o.

604
00:54:36,606 --> 00:54:38,066
‎Don't ever say that.

605
00:54:41,361 --> 00:54:43,822
‎This is all on me. Everything is my fault.

606
00:54:45,865 --> 00:54:48,326
‎People used to point fingers at me…

607
00:54:51,287 --> 00:54:52,956
‎but then I found a treasure like you.

608
00:54:53,957 --> 00:54:54,916
‎"Look."

609
00:54:55,000 --> 00:54:58,086
‎"The son I gave birth to
‎is a gift sent to me from God."

610
00:54:58,670 --> 00:55:00,255
‎"Mock me all you want."

611
00:55:01,756 --> 00:55:04,384
‎"I know it's just jealousy talking."

612
00:55:05,510 --> 00:55:07,595
‎I wanted to brag about you
‎and lord it over them.

613
00:55:08,763 --> 00:55:11,266
‎That's why I was so harsh with you.

614
00:55:11,891 --> 00:55:14,728
‎You never said a word of complaint,

615
00:55:14,811 --> 00:55:16,771
‎but I kept pushing you harder.

616
00:55:21,651 --> 00:55:22,610
‎I'm sorry.

617
00:55:26,197 --> 00:55:28,700
‎I wanted to help your music career.

618
00:55:29,534 --> 00:55:31,327
‎But I ended up becoming a huge obstacle.

619
00:55:33,496 --> 00:55:35,040
‎Forget about me now.

620
00:55:35,123 --> 00:55:37,167
‎Cut ties with me and go live your life.

621
00:55:38,126 --> 00:55:39,586
‎Just spread your wings

622
00:55:40,253 --> 00:55:42,589
‎and focus on the music you love.

623
00:55:47,844 --> 00:55:50,597
‎You must've been sick of living as my son.

624
00:55:51,765 --> 00:55:53,099
‎I'm sick of it too.

625
00:55:56,478 --> 00:55:57,854
‎Living as your mom.

626
00:57:19,686 --> 00:57:21,354
‎Continuing from yesterday,

627
00:57:21,438 --> 00:57:25,400
‎we will be rehearsing the ‎Lacrimosa
‎from Mozart's Requiem.

628
00:57:26,526 --> 00:57:27,777
‎As you know,

629
00:57:28,820 --> 00:57:32,282
‎this was the last piece
‎Mozart worked on before his death.

630
00:57:33,700 --> 00:57:36,119
‎Every note is heavy with grief and pain,

631
00:57:36,202 --> 00:57:39,873
‎as if he foresaw his own death.

632
00:57:42,959 --> 00:57:46,546
‎That is why the violins
‎should sound like falling teardrops,

633
00:57:47,255 --> 00:57:50,008
‎as the title ‎Lacrimosa‎ suggests.

634
00:57:51,885 --> 00:57:53,344
‎And the choir

635
00:57:53,428 --> 00:57:55,930
‎should carefully build tension

636
00:57:56,681 --> 00:57:59,517
‎in a slow, gradual rise,

637
00:58:00,101 --> 00:58:03,480
‎like someone approaching
‎the judgment seat.

638
00:58:30,256 --> 00:58:36,471
‎-Full of tears
‎-Full of tears

639
00:58:36,554 --> 00:58:43,353
‎-Will be that day
‎-Will be that day

640
00:58:43,436 --> 00:58:49,859
‎-When from the ashes
‎-When from the ashes

641
00:58:49,943 --> 00:58:56,324
‎-Shall arise
‎-Shall arise

642
00:58:56,407 --> 00:59:03,122
‎-The guilty man
‎-The guilty man

643
00:59:03,206 --> 00:59:09,963
‎-To be judged
‎-To be judged

644
00:59:10,046 --> 00:59:16,386
‎-Full of tears
‎-Full of tears

645
00:59:16,469 --> 00:59:21,975
‎-Will be that day
‎-Will be that day

646
00:59:23,142 --> 00:59:29,482
‎-When from the ashes
‎-When from the ashes

647
00:59:29,566 --> 00:59:36,239
‎-Shall arise
‎-Shall arise

648
00:59:36,322 --> 00:59:42,537
‎-The guilty man
‎-The guilty man

649
00:59:42,620 --> 00:59:48,918
‎-To be judged
‎-To be judged

650
00:59:49,002 --> 00:59:55,883
‎-Therefore spare him
‎-Therefore spare him

651
00:59:55,967 --> 01:00:01,848
‎-O God
‎-O God

652
01:00:01,931 --> 01:00:08,855
‎-Merciful Lord Jesus
‎-Merciful Lord Jesus

653
01:00:09,647 --> 01:00:12,525
‎SPECIAL THANKS TO KO CHANG-SEOK
‎FOR HIS GUEST APPEARANCE

654
01:00:32,962 --> 01:00:35,089
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

655
01:00:35,173 --> 01:00:39,052
‎Who'd have known such a powerful family
‎would end up in ruins like this?

656
01:00:39,135 --> 01:00:41,137
‎Our project is over now, right?

657
01:00:41,220 --> 01:00:42,597
‎I'll never play again.

658
01:00:43,097 --> 01:00:46,351
‎All of this happened because of my greed.

659
01:00:47,185 --> 01:00:48,102
‎Come with me.

660
01:00:48,186 --> 01:00:49,103
‎I want to show you something.

661
01:00:49,771 --> 01:00:52,732
‎All we can do is just keep making music.

662
01:00:52,815 --> 01:00:53,775
‎Play freely…

663
01:00:54,484 --> 01:00:55,610
‎like that day.

664
01:00:55,693 --> 01:00:59,947
‎Jeong-yo put in his resignation
‎and won't answer his phone.

665
01:01:00,031 --> 01:01:02,116
‎And do me one last favor.

666
01:01:03,117 --> 01:01:08,122
‎Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
